\n    \\[ g(kc) = 2014k \\]\n\n3. Setting \\( n = -c \\), we have:\n    \\[ g(f(m) - c) + g(m) = g(-c) + g(3m) + 2014 \\]\n    With \\( g(-c) = -2014 \\), we can write:\n    \\[ g(f(m) - c) + g(m) = g(3m) + 2014 - 2014 = g(3m) \\]\n\n    Therefore:\n    \\[ g(f(m) - c) = g(3m) - g(m) \\]\n\n4. Since \\( g(n + c) = g(n) + 2014 \\), we replace \\( n \\) by \\( n-c \\):\n    \\[ g(g(m) + n) = g(g(m)) + g(n) \\]\n\n5. Setting \\( m = c \\), we obtain \\( g(c) = 2014 \\), making:\n    \\[ g(n + 2014) = g(n) + g(2014) \\]\n\n    Since \\( g(n + 2014c) = g(n) + 2014^2 \\), we then have:\n    \\[ c \\cdot g(2014) = 2014^2 \\]\n\n6. Set \\( n = c \\) and simplify to get:\n    \\[ g(2014 + 2c) = 4 \\times 2014 \\]\n    This simplifies to \\( g(2014) = 2 \\times 2014 \\), so \\( c = 1007 \\).\n\n7. We now have:\n    \\[ g(n + 1007) = g(n) + 2014 \\]\n    and\n    \\[ g(1007k) = 2014k \\]\n\n8. For \\( g(1007g(m)) = 2014g(m) \\):\n    \\[ g(k \\cdot g(m)) = k \\cdot g(g(m)) \\]\n    leading to:\n    \\[ g(1007g(m)) = 1007g(g(m)) \\]\n    Therefore:\n    \\[ g(g(m)) = 2g(m) \\]\n    and:\n    \\[ g(3m) = 3g(m) \\]\n\n9. Therefore, we conclude that \\( g(n) = 2n \\) for all integers \\( n \\).\n\nHence, substituting back, we obtain:\n\\[ f(n) = g(n) + c = 2n + 1007 \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[ \\boxed{f(n) = 2n + 1007} \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Given that the complex number \\( z \\) satisfies \\( |z| = 1 \\), what is the maximum value of \\( \\left|z^{3} - 3z - 2 \\right| \\)?", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to find the maximum value of |z\u00b3 - 3z - 2| where |z| = 1. Hmm, let's start by recalling that if |z| = 1, then z is a complex number on the unit circle in the complex plane. That means we can represent z as e^{i\u03b8} where \u03b8 is the argument of z, right? So maybe I can express everything in terms of \u03b8 and then find the maximum value of the modulus.\n\nLet me write z = e^{i\u03b8