tes) between buses from each terminal.\n\n2. **Relative Speed Analysis:**\n   - **Oncoming buses (head-on):** Relative speed = \\( v_b + v_h \\).\n   - **Buses overtaking from behind:** Relative speed = \\( v_b - v_h \\).\n\n3. **Distance Between Buses:**\n   - Buses depart every \\( T \\) minutes, so the distance between consecutive buses in one direction is \\( D = v_b \\cdot T \\).\n\n4. **Time Between Encounters:**\n   - **Head-on buses:** Time interval = \\( \\frac{D}{v_b + v_h} = 6 \\) minutes.\n   - **Overtaking buses:** Time interval = \\( \\frac{D}{v_b - v_h} = 12 \\) minutes.\n\n5. **Set Up Equations:**\n   - From head-on: \\( \\frac{v_b T}{v_b + v_h} = 6 \\)  ...(1)\n   - From overtaking: \\( \\frac{v_b T}{v_b - v_h} = 12 \\) ...(2)\n\n6. **Solve for \\( v_b \\) in Terms of \\( v_h \\):**\n   - Divide Equation (2) by Equation (1):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{v_b + v_h}{v_b - v_h} = 2 \\implies v_b = 3v_h\n     \\]\n   - Substitute \\( v_b = 3v_h \\) into Equation (1):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{3v_h \\cdot T}{4v_h} = 6 \\implies \\frac{3T}{4} = 6 \\implies T = 8\n     \\]\n\n**Conclusion:** The buses are dispatched every **8 minutes**.", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Given Information and Setup:**\n   - Xiaoming encounters a \"Chunhui Cup\" car every 6 minutes from the opposite direction.\n   - Xiaoming is overtaken by a \"Chunhui Cup\" car every 12 minutes.\n   - Chunhui Cup cars operate at a constant speed and stop at regular intervals to pick up passengers.\n\n2. **Determine the Least Common Multiple (LCM):**\n   - The least common multiple of 6 minutes and 12 minutes is 12 minutes.\n   - Therefore, consider Xiaoming's movement over a 12-minute period. \n\n3. **Opposite Direction Encounters:**\n   - In 12 minutes, Xiaoming encounters:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{12}{6} = 2 \\text{ cars} \\quad \\text{from the opposite direction}.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Same Direction Overtakes:**\n   - In 12 minutes, Xiaoming is overtaken by:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{12}{12} = 1 \\text{ car} \\qu