\):  \n\\[\nf(0) = \\sqrt{0^2 - 5(0) + 4} = \\sqrt{4} = 2\n\\]  \n**Answer:** \\( \\boxed{2} \\)\n\nb) **When \\( x = a + 1 \\):**  \nSubstitute \\( x = a + 1 \\):  \n\\[\nf(a + 1) = \\sqrt{(a + 1)^2 - 5(a + 1) + 4}\n\\]  \nExpand and simplify:  \n\\[\n(a + 1)^2 - 5(a + 1) + 4 = a^2 - 3a\n\\]  \nThus,  \n\\[\nf(a + 1) = \\sqrt{a^2 - 3a}\n\\]  \n**Answer:** \\( \\boxed{\\sqrt{a^2 - 3a}} \\)\n\n---\n\n**2) \\( \\varphi(x) = 2 \\arcsin x + \\operatorname{arctg} 2x \\) when \\( x = -\\frac{1}{2} \\):**\n\n- Compute \\( 2 \\arcsin\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\):  \n  \\[\n  \\arcsin\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\implies 2\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = -\\frac{\\pi}{3}\n  \\]\n\n- Compute \\( \\operatorname{arctg}(2 \\cdot -\\frac{1}{2}) = \\operatorname{arctg}(-1) \\):  \n  \\[\n  \\operatorname{arctg}(-1) = -\\frac{\\pi}{4}\n  \\]\n\nSum the results:  \n\\[\n\\varphi\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = -\\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = -\\frac{7\\pi}{12}\n\\]  \n**Answer:** \\( \\boxed{-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12}} \\)\n\n---\n\n**3) \\( y = x^2 \\arccos \\frac{x}{2} - 3x \\operatorname{arcctg} x \\) when \\( x = -1 \\):**\n\n- Compute \\( x^2 \\arccos\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) \\):  \n  \\[\n  (-1)^2 = 1, \\quad \\arccos\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} \\implies 1 \\cdot \\frac{2\\pi}{3} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}\n  \\]\n\n- Compute \\( -3x \\operatorname{arcctg} x \\):  \n  \\[\n  \\operatorname{arcctg}(-1) = \\frac{3\\pi}{4}, \\quad -3(-1) \\cdot \\frac{3\\pi}{4} = \\frac{9\\pi}{4}\n  \\]\n\nCombine the terms:  \n\\[\ny = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} + \\frac{9\\pi}{4} = \\frac{8\\pi}{12} + \\frac{27\\pi}{12} = \\frac{35\\pi}{12}\n\\]  \n**Answer:** \\( \\boxed{\\dfrac{35\\pi}{12}} \\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n\n1. For the function \\( f(x) = \\sqrt{x^2 - 5x + 4} \\):\n\n   a) When \\( x = 0 \\):\n\n   \\[\n   f(0) = \\sqrt{0^2 - 5 \\cdot 0 + 4} = \\sqrt{4} = 2\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, the particular value of the function \\( f(x) \\) at 