isfies x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 = r\u00b2 - d\u00b2, then we are done.\n\nAlternatively, since the circle with diameter AB is the set of all points P such that angle APB is a right angle (by Thales' theorem), maybe there's a way to use that property. But perhaps coordinates are more straightforward.\n\nLet me proceed with coordinates. Let\u2019s parametrize the secant line passing through A. Let's define the secant line by a slope. Let\u2019s say the secant line through A has a slope m. Then, its equation is y - \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = m(x - 0), so y = mx + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2).\n\nThis line intersects circle O1: (x + d)^2 + y^2 = r\u00b2\n\nSubstituting y = mx + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2):\n\n(x + d)^2 + (mx + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))^2 = r\u00b2\n\nExpanding this:\n\n(x\u00b2 + 2xd + d\u00b2) + (m\u00b2x\u00b2 + 2mx\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = r\u00b2\n\nCombine terms:\n\nx\u00b2 + 2xd + d\u00b2 + m\u00b2x\u00b2 + 2mx\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + r\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nSimplify:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 + 2xd + 2mx\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + d\u00b2 + r\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nFurther simplifying:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 + 2x(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) + r\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nSubtract r\u00b2 from both sides:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 + 2x(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) = 0\n\nFactor out x:\n\nx[(1 + m\u00b2)x + 2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))] = 0\n\nSo, the solutions are x=0 (which corresponds to point A) and x = -2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2)\n\nSimilarly, for circle O2: (x - d)^2 + y\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nSubstituting y = mx + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2):\n\n(x - d)^2 + (mx + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nExpanding:\n\nx\u00b2 - 2xd + d\u00b2 + m\u00b2x\u00b2 + 2mx\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + r\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nCombine terms:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 - 2xd + 2mx\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + d\u00b2 + r\u00b2 - d\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nSimplify:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 + 2x(-d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) + r\u00b2 = r\u00b2\n\nSubtract r\u00b2:\n\n(1 + m\u00b2)x\u00b2 + 2x(-d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) = 0\n\nFactor:\n\nx[(1 + m\u00b2)x + 2(-d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))] = 0\n\nSolutions are x=0 (point A) and x = 2(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2)\n\nTherefore, the secant line intersects circle O1 at A (0, \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) and point C with x-coordinate -2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2), and circle O2 at A and point D with x-coordinate 2(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2).\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of points C and D are:\n\nC: ( -2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2), m*(-2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2)) + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) )\n\nSimplify the y-coordinate for C:\n\ny = -2m(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2) + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)\n\nSimilarly, point D has coordinates:\n\nD: ( 2(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2), m*(2(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2)) + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) )\n\nSimplify the y-coordinate for D:\n\ny = 2m(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2) + \u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)\n\nNow, we need to find the midpoint M of segment CD. Let's compute the average of the x-coordinates and the y-coordinates.\n\nFirst, the x-coordinate of M:\n\nx_M = [ -2(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2) + 2(d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))/(1 + m\u00b2) ] / 2\n\nFactor out 2/(1 + m\u00b2):\n\nx_M = [ 2/(1 + m\u00b2) * ( - (d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) + (d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) ) ] / 2\n\nSimplify inside the brackets:\n\n- d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) + d - m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2) = -2m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)\n\nThus:\n\nx_M = [ 2/(1 + m\u00b2) * (-2m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)) ] / 2 = [ -4m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)/(1 + m\u00b2) ] / 2 = -2m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2)/(1 + m\u00b2)\n\nNow, the y-coordinate of M:\n\ny_M = [ y_C + y_D ] / 2\n\nCompute y_C + y_D:\n\n[ -2m(d + m\u221a(r\u00b2 - d\u00b2))