n\nTherefore, if we can prove that m_a m_b m_c \u2265 \u0394 s, then the result follows.\n\nNow, how to prove that m_a m_b m_c \u2265 \u0394 s?\n\nLet me express both sides in terms of the sides a, b, c.\n\nFirst, recall that \u0394 = \u221a[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)]\n\nAnd s = (a + b + c)/2.\n\nSo \u0394 s = s \u221a[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)]\n\nOn the other hand, m_a m_b m_c = product of the medians.\n\nFrom Apollonius's theorem, each median is given by:\n\nm_a = (1/2)\u221a(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)\n\nSimilarly for m_b and m_c.\n\nThus, m_a m_b m_c = (1/8)\u221a[(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2)]\n\nTherefore, we need to show that:\n\n(1/8)\u221a[(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2)] \u2265 \u221a[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)] * s\n\nSquare both sides to eliminate the square roots:\n\n(1/64)(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2) \u2265 s\u00b2 s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)\n\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\ns^3 (s - a)(s - b)(s - c)\n\nRecall that Heron's formula states \u0394\u00b2 = s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c), so s^3 (s - a)(s - b)(s - c) = s^3 * \u0394\u00b2 / s = s\u00b2 \u0394\u00b2\n\nTherefore, the inequality becomes:\n\n(1/64)(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2) \u2265 s\u00b2 \u0394\u00b2\n\nMultiply both sides by 64:\n\n(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2) \u2265 64 s\u00b2 \u0394\u00b2\n\nNow, substitute \u0394\u00b2 = s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c):\n\n= 64 s\u00b2 * s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c) = 64 s^3 (s - a)(s - b)(s - c)\n\nTherefore, need to show:\n\n(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2)(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2) \u2265 64 s^3 (s - a)(s - b)(s - c)\n\nThis seems like a complicated identity, but perhaps expanding both sides might help.\n\nAlternatively, express everything in terms of Ravi variables x, y, z, where a = y + z, b = z + x, c = x + y. Then s = x + y + z.\n\nLet me substitute:\n\nFirst, compute the left-hand side:\n\n(2b\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - a\u00b2) = 2(z + x)^2 + 2(x + y)^2 - (y + z)^2\n\nAs before, expand:\n\n2(z\u00b2 + 2zx + x\u00b2) + 2(x\u00b2 + 2xy + y\u00b2) - (y\u00b2 + 2yz + z\u00b2)\n\n= 2z\u00b2 + 4zx + 2x\u00b2 + 2x\u00b2 + 4xy + 2y\u00b2 - y\u00b2 - 2yz - z\u00b2\n\n= z\u00b2 + 4zx + 4x\u00b2 + 4xy + y\u00b2 - 2yz\n\nSimilarly, the other terms:\n\n(2a\u00b2 + 2c\u00b2 - b\u00b2) = 2(y + z)^2 + 2(x + y)^2 - (z + x)^2\n\nExpand:\n\n2(y\u00b2 + 2yz + z\u00b2) + 2(x\u00b2 + 2xy + y\u00b2) - (z\u00b2 + 2zx + x\u00b2)\n\n= 2y\u00b2 + 4yz + 2z\u00b2 + 2x\u00b2 + 4xy + 2y\u00b2 - z\u00b2 - 2zx - x\u00b2\n\n= y\u00b2 + 4yz + z\u00b2 + x\u00b2 + 4xy + 2y\u00b2 - 2zx\n\nWait, let me compute step by step:\n\nFirst term: 2(y\u00b2 + 2yz + z\u00b2) = 2y\u00b2 + 4yz + 2z\u00b2\n\nSecond term: 2(x\u00b2 + 2xy + y\u00b2) = 2x\u00b2 + 4xy + 2y\u00b2\n\nThird term: - (z\u00b2 + 2zx + x\u00b2) = -z\u00b2 - 2zx - x\u00b2\n\nCombine all terms:\n\ny\u00b2 terms: 2y\u00b2 + 2y\u00b2 = 4y\u00b2\n\nyz terms: 4yz\n\nz\u00b2 terms: 2z\u00b2 - z\u00b2 = z\u00b2\n\nx\u00b2 terms: 2x\u00b2 - x\u00b2 = x\u00b2\n\nxy terms: 4xy\n\nzx terms: -2zx\n\nThus, overall:\n\n4y\u00b2 + 4yz + z\u00b2 + x\u00b2 + 4xy - 2zx\n\nSimilarly, the third factor:\n\n(2a\u00b2 + 2b\u00b2 - c\u00b2) = 2(y + z)^2 + 2(z + x)^2 - (x + y)^2\n\nExpand:\n\n2(y\u00b2 + 2yz + z\u00b2) + 2(z\u00b2 + 2zx + x\u00b2) - (x\u00b2 + 2xy + y\u00b2)\n\n= 2y\u00b2 + 4yz + 2z\u00b2 + 2z\u00b2 + 4zx + 2x\u00b2 - x\u00b2 - 2xy - y\u00b2\n\nCombine terms:\n\ny\u00b2: 2y\u00b2 - y\u00b2 = y\u00b2\n\nyz: 4yz\n\nz\u00b2: 2z\u00b2 + 2z\u00b2 = 4z\u00b2\n\nzx: 4zx\n\nx\u00b2: 2x\u00b2 - x\u00b2 = x\u00b2\n\nxy: -2xy\n\nThus, overall:\n\ny\u00b2 + 4yz + 4z\u00b2 + 4zx + x\u00b2 - 2xy\n\nTherefore, the left-hand side of the inequality is:\n\n[z\u00b2 + 4zx + 4x\u00b2 + 4xy + y\u00b2 -